menu "upload_auth: /scripts upload authentication (DESIGN.md §10)"

    config UPLOAD_AUTH_ECDSA_PUBLIC_KEY
        string "Hex-encoded P-256 public key for /scripts/* upload signatures (empty disables auth entirely)"
        default ""
        help
            If empty (the default), upload authentication is not wired in
            at all - no nonce endpoint is registered and /scripts/* accepts
            uploads exactly as if this component didn't exist, fine for a
            trusted-LAN deployment (DESIGN.md §1). Set this to the
            uploader's ECDSA P-256 public key to require a valid nonce plus
            an ECDSA-SHA256 signature on every upload (DESIGN.md §10). The
            matching private key never has to touch the device - keep it
            wherever `tools/upload_script.sh` runs.

            130 hex characters: the uncompressed SEC1 point encoding (the
            byte 0x04 followed by the 32-byte X and 32-byte Y coordinates).
            For a standard P-256 key pair:

                openssl ecparam -name prime256v1 -genkey -noout -out key.pem
                openssl ec -in key.pem -pubout -out pub.pem
                openssl ec -pubin -in pub.pem -outform DER | tail -c 65 | xxd -p -c200

endmenu
